<article class="env-lemma" id="0DFV">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0DFV">Lemma <span data-tag="0DFV">84.3.1</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $\tau \in \{ {\acute{e}tale}, fppf, ph\} $ (add more here). The inclusion functor </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  (\mathit{Sch}/S)_\tau \longrightarrow (\textit{Spaces}/S)_\tau  \]
</div>
  <p> is a special cocontinuous functor (Sites, Definition <a href="/tag/03CG" data-tag="03CG">7.29.2</a>) and hence identifies topoi. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      The conditions of Sites, Lemma <a href="/tag/03A0" data-tag="03A0">7.29.1</a> are immediately verified as our functor is fully faithful and as every algebraic space has an étale covering by schemes. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>